    "commonMistakes": [
      "Thinking rubber is more elastic because it stretches more.",
      "Changing $Y$ when geometry changes.",
      "Dropping the $\\frac{1}{2}$ in $U = \\frac{1}{2}F\\Delta L$.",
      "Making thermal stress depend on $L$.",
      "Sign confusion in Poisson's ratio (lateral contraction).",
      "Using $\\sigma\\varepsilon$ (missing the $\\frac{1}{2}$) for energy density.",
      "Mixing $K$ (bulk) with $k$ (spring constant).",
      "Rushing the final unit conversion after a correct setup."
    ],
    "examChecklist": [
